<title>USA: Cleveland-Cliffs sees 1997 record production.</title>
<headline>Cleveland-Cliffs sees 1997 record production.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cleveland-Cliffs Inc said on Tuesday that record 1997 production is scheduled and over 85 percent of its sales capacity is committed on multi-year contracts.</p>
<p>Industry analysts are expecting strong North American Steel production and shipments in 1997, Cleveland-Cliffs said. The six North American mines the company operates are scheduled to operate near full capacity in 1997 and produce a record 41.7 million tons of ore.</p>
<p>Cleveland-Cliffs said its share of scheduled production amounts to 10.8 million tons.</p>
</text>
